  "explanation": "Combined regime: the province offers unusually strong state-level non-discrimination, constitutional, hate-crime and care protections, and its own facilities ban is not documented. Those protections do not control the traveller-facing federal layer: birth-sex passport processing, entry officers instructed to refuse on document discrepancy and consider permanent fraud ineligibility, birth-sex exclusion in federal single-sex facilities, and documented severe abuse and hormone denial in federal custody. Federal threat-framing and unresolved litigation add uncertainty, especially for minors seeking care or competing. State remedies materially help in hotels and state services but cannot cancel border, federal-facility or federal-custody exposure.",
  "factor_matrix": {
    "entry_documents": {
