    "investigation_detention_custody": {
      "exposure": "Federal immigration custody reports describe forced labour, beatings, solitary confinement and severe sexual abuse of trans men; federal corrections from 2026 reportedly cut hair, removed hormones and substituted psychiatric treatment. State custody is explicitly protected by 2023 law, yet the July 2026 assessment finds shortfalls in incarcerated trans protections.",
      "protection": "State correctional-protection legislation and a national hate-crime statute provide some legal basis for complaints; several federal orders have been enjoined, though custody policies' current operative scope is contested.",
      "interaction": "Entry fraud suspicion is the main route into federal custody, where state protections and state inspectors have no authority; hormone denial and abuse are therefore the operative final stage despite state law.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "federal_state_facilities": {
      "exposure": "A federal order bars trans people from government-funded single-sex facilities congruent with identity; many states impose broader bans and four make some use criminal under specified circumstances, including refusal to depart after being asked.",
      "protection": "The province prohibits gender-identity discrimination in public accommodation, employment and housing and added gender identity to its constitutional equal-protection clause by voter referendum; no province-specific facilities ban is reproduced in the dossier.",
      "interaction": "State public-accommodation protection may govern hotels and state premises, but it does not pre-empt federal buildings or federal facilities rules; the province facilities entry itself is uncertain.",
      "status": "uncertain"
    },
    "care_services": {
      "exposure": "National measures restrict or threaten funding and coverage connected to gender-affirming care, propose barring public-insurance reimbursement under 18, and direct investigation/prosecution concerning minors' social transition; several orders are blocked or in litigation. Emergency-care practice for a trans visitor is not separately documented.",
      "protection": "Province insurers, including its public programme, must cover medically necessary gender-affirming treatments from 2024; a broader care-shield bill was vetoed in 2023 and the July 2026 assessment notes healthcare-equity shortfalls.",
      "interaction": "State coverage helps an adult obtaining planned care in the province, but federal funding, insurance and child-care rules can still affect continuity, records and a travelling minor's treatment.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
