      "exposure": "Passport and executive-order challenges remain unresolved, several measures are enjoined, and the dossier leaves province bathroom rules, airport handling, visitor emergency-care practice and the size of healthcare/custody shortfalls unresolved.",
      "protection": "The July 2026 assessment places the province in its low-risk group, one tier below the most-protective tier, crediting robust non-discrimination policies; state courts and the constitution provide functioning local remedies.",
      "interaction": "Local remedies are meaningful for state services and private discrimination, but no documented pre-emption, immunity or refusal makes them cancel federal entry, facilities or custody authority.",
      "status": "documented"
